The alcohol is reacted with a mixture of sodium iodide and concentrated phosphoric acid, {H}_{3}{\mathrm{PO}}_{4}$, and the iodoalkane is distilled off. The 2-iodobutane formed in the previous reaction give Grignard reagent with magnesium metal in dry ether. The Grignard reagent formed reacts with {D}_{2}O$ to give 2-deuterobutane.

